The chat shows the agent it is bound to: a chat with a new agent no longer
reads "Caelza Agent", so the owner can tell their own agent from Cael, the
setup guide, at a glance.

Two places said the product's name where the agent's belonged: the top bar's
title on /agent/<alias> was the section's "Agent" right beside the Caelza
wordmark, and an empty chat's heading was the string "Caelza Agent". Now the
top bar's title is the agent's look and "Chat with <name>"; the empty chat's
heading is the agent's name, with a line saying whether this is the owner's
own agent (and where Cael is) or Cael himself; the chat pane's header shows
the name larger, its look beside it; the browser tab reads "<name> · Chat".

The chat workspace mirrors the tab in front to the address bar with
replaceState, which the router does not see, so it reports the agent in front
through `lib/activeChat.ts` (overlay) and the top bar and the tab title read
that, not the stale address. The overlay holds the logic
(`lib/activeChat.logic.ts`, its test in the web test list); this patch
touches the chat header and empty state (AgentChat.tsx), the workspace
(ChatWorkspace.tsx), the top bar (Header.tsx), the tab title (Layout.tsx),
the strings (i18n.ts) and the test list (package.json).

